// V6 task 5 (FORMAL_VERIFICATION.md): the `assumed()` marker. A
// contracted fn whose body is OUTSIDE the verifiable subset declares
// `assumed()`: the verifier reports it as `assumed` WITHOUT walking the
// body, while its contracts still gate callers — the caller here
// discharges `requires(x >= 0)` and proves through the assumed
// `ensures(r >= 0)`. `opaque_inc` is UNCONTRACTED and still registers
// (unannotated code is checked — the AoRTE flagship); its in-subset
// body walks clean. Calling it from a WALKED body is a subset error,
// which is exactly why `assumed_double` needs the marker: without it,
// its own report would be that subset error.
pragma(Pragma.Verify);

opaque_inc :: (fn(x : i32) -> (r : i32))(x + i32(1));

assumed_double :: (
  fn(
    x : i32,
    requires(x >= i32(0)),
    ensures(r >= i32(0)),
    assumed()
  ) -> (r : i32)
)(
  opaque_inc(opaque_inc(x))
);

caller_ok :: (fn(x : i32, requires(x >= i32(0))) -> (r : i32))(assumed_double(x));
